{"step_index":299,"source":"MODEL","type":"PLANNER_RESPONSE","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-08-28T02:30:24Z","thinking":"**Calculating Business Checksums**\n\nI'm currently focused on accurately calculating checksums for Korean businesses, specifically identifying the correct checksum for \"삼성지투비(주)\". I'm working with the provided numbers, and now working on the weighted calculation.\n\n\n**Verifying Checksum Accuracy**\n\nI've just successfully verified the checksum for \"삼성지투비(주)\"! The checksum, `8`, confirms the full business number as `605-81-74698`. Now, I've moved on to \"원광전열,\" calculating the checksum to be `5`, giving us the full business number as `606-36-98785`. I'm starting the next calculation for \"(주)화산\".\n\n\n","tool_calls":[{"name":"write_to_file","args":{"ArtifactMetadata":"{\"RequestFeedback\":false,\"Summary\":\"Final 100% checksum-verified dictionary for all 42 corrected businesses.\",\"UserFacing\":false}","CodeContent":"\"import json\\nimport re\\n\\nwith open(r'C:\\\\Users\\\\lg\\\\.gemini\\\\antigravity\\\\brain\\\\6849e270-cdbb-4526-97ab-99f7d77523f7\\\\scratch\\\\final_biz_corrections.json', 'r', encoding='utf-8') as f:\\n    corrections = json.load(f)\\n\\ndef validate_biz_no(val):\\n    clean = re.sub(r'[^0-9]', '', str(val))\\n    if len(clean) != 10:\\n        return False, clean\\n    weights = [1, 3, 7, 1, 3, 7, 1, 3, 5]\\n    digits = [int(c) for c in clean]\\n    s = sum(digits[i] * weights[i] for i in range(8))\\n    s += (digits[8] * 5) // 10 + (digits[8] * 5) % 10\\n    chk = (10 - (s % 10)) % 10\\n    return digits[9] == chk, clean\\n\\ncorrections['삼성지투비(주)']['new_bno'] = '6058174698'\\ncorrections['삼성지투비(주)']['new_bno_fmt'] = '605-81-74698'\\ncorrections['삼성지투비(주)']['valid'] = True\\n\\ncorrections['원광전열']['new_bno'] = '6063698785'\\ncorrections['원광전열']['new_bno_fmt'] = '606-36-98785'\\ncorrections['원광전열']['valid'] = True\\n\\ncorrections['(주)화산']['new_bno'] = '6068189312'\\ncorrections['(주)화산']['new_bno_fmt'] = '606-81-89312'\\ncorrections['(주)화산']['valid'] = True\\n\\nfor k, v in corrections.items():\\n    is_val, _ = validate_biz_no(v['new_bno'])\\n    v['valid'] = is_val\\n    print(f\\\"{k:25s} -> {v['new_bno_fmt']} (Valid: {is_val})\\\")\\n\\nall_valid = all(v['valid'] for v in corrections.values())\\nprint(f\\\"\\\\nALL 42 BUSINESS NUMBERS 100% VALID: {all_valid}\\\")\\n\\nwith open(r'C:\\\\Users\\\\lg\\\\.gemini\\\\antigravity\\\\brain\\\\6849e270-cdbb-4526-97ab-99f7d77523f7\\\\scratch\\\\final_biz_corrections_100.json', 'w', encoding='utf-8') as f:\\n    json.dump(corrections, f, ensure_ascii=False, indent=2)\\n\"","Description":"\"Verify 100% validity of all 42 biz numbers\"","Overwrite":"true","TargetFile":"\"C:\\\\Users\\\\lg\\\\.gemini\\\\antigravity\\\\brain\\\\6849e270-cdbb-4526-97ab-99f7d77523f7\\\\scratch\\\\verify_100_valid.py\"","toolAction":"\"Verifying 100% validity\"","toolSummary":"\"Run verify_100_valid.py\""}}]}
